  "adaptations": {
    "components.css": "Canonical rules run in the Tailwind components layer; app table links/selection and responsive hit areas extend the shared styles. This makes visibility/size utilities work without changing canonical tokens.",
    "BfDialog.tsx": "Existing approved app superset: accessible title/description IDs and dismiss behavior.",
    "BfDataTable.tsx": "Existing app superset: semantic row links, selection, controlled sorting; canonical 16px native checkbox with 32px labelled click target that does not activate the row.",
    "tokens.css": "Byte-identical canonical tokens; no local palette or typography reinterpretation.",
    "BfCombobox.tsx": "Canonical appearance and placement rules retained; option lists portal into their owning native dialog so mobile bulk-action menus remain in the browser top layer."
  },
  "integration_notes": [
    "Canonical tokens are byte-identical. Component stylesheet rules retain canonical values and are placed in the CSS components layer so Tailwind responsive utilities apply.",
    "Imports precede CSS rules; compiled output includes canonical tokens without external token stylesheet requests.",
    "App table/dialog supersets retain the canonical appearance and add existing app behavior. Action menus have viewport-bounded scrolling; compact controls have usable touch targets."
  ],
